  "before_interfaces": {
    "def-qftx-localized-equivariant-borel-moore-data": [
      null,
      "## Definition\n\nAssume the Axiom of Choice. Let $r\\geq 0$, let $T=(\\mathbb C^\\times)^r$ act algebraically on a separated finite-type complex variety $X$, and suppose $X$ has a finite cover by $T$-invariant affine open subvarieties. Use rational coefficients. Let $K=(S^1)^r$ be the maximal compact subgroup of $T$, and use the product right Milnor model $E_K=(E_{S^1})^r$, $B_K=E_K/K=(\\mathbb{CP}^{\\infty})^r$. The inclusion $K\\subset T$ gives the same topological Borel construction up to homotopy. For each algebraic character $\\chi:T\\to\\mathbb C^\\times$, let $L_\\chi=E_K\\times_K\\mathbb C_{\\chi|_K}\\to B_K$, with right equivalence $(e,z)\\cdot t=(e\\cdot t,\\chi(t)^{-1}z)$, and put $u_\\chi=c_1(L_\\chi)$. For the coordinate characters $\\chi_i$ and $u_i=u_{\\chi_i}$, the coefficient ring is $R_T=H^*(B_K;\\mathbb Q)=\\mathbb Q[u_1,\\ldots,u_r]$, with $|u_i|=2$ and $u_\\chi=\\sum_i n_i u_i$ for $\\chi(t_1,\\ldots,t_r)=\\prod_i t_i^{n_i}$. Let $S_T$ be the multiplicative set consisting of $1$ and finite products of $u_\\chi$ for nontrivial $\\chi$.\n\nLet $H^{\\mathrm{BM},T}_j(X;\\mathbb Q)=\\operatorname{Hom}_{D^b_{T,c}(X;\\mathbb Q)}(\\mathbb Q_X,\\omega_X^T[-j])$, where $\\omega_X^T$ is the normalized equivariant dualizing object whose restriction is the ordinary dualizing object $\\omega_X$, without a quotient-stack dimension shift. Equivalently, this is the stable value in degree $j$ of $H^{\\mathrm{BM}}_{j+2rm}(X_m;\\mathbb Q)$, where $U_m=(\\mathbb C^{m+1}\\setminus\\{0\\})^r$ has the free right scalar $T$-action, $X_m=(U_m\\times X)/T$ uses $(e,x)\\cdot t=(e\\cdot t,t^{-1}\\cdot x)$, and the supplied bounded-Hom comparison is taken in its stable range. The ring $R_T$ acts by pullback from $B_K$ and cap product. For an $R_T$-module $M$, $S_T^{-1}M$ consists of fractions $m/s$ with $m\\in M$, $s\\in S_T$, and $m/s=m'/s'$ exactly when some $t\\in S_T$ satisfies $t(s'm-sm')=0$; addition and scalar multiplication are the induced fraction operations. Proper equivariant maps induce degree-preserving pushforwards, invariant open inclusions induce Borel–Moore restrictions, and a smooth pure $d$-dimensional complex variety has its complex-oriented fundamental class $[X]_T$ in degree $2d$. For $r=0$, $R_T=\\mathbb Q$ and $S_T=\\{1\\}$."
    ],
    "lem-qftx-eigenfunction-open-bm-annihilation": [
      null,
      "## Statement\n\nLet $T=(\\mathbb C^\\times)^r$ act algebraically on a separated finite-type complex variety $X$ with a finite invariant affine open cover. Let $U$ be one affine chart, let $f\\in\\mathcal O(U)$ be regular with a nontrivial character $\\chi:T\\to\\mathbb C^\\times$, and fix the convention $f(t\\cdot x)=\\chi(t)f(x)$. If $D(f)=\\{x\\in U:f(x)\\neq0\\}$ is nonempty, then the equivariant character class $u_\\chi=c_1(L_{\\chi|_K})$ acts by zero on every group $H^{\\mathrm{BM},T}_j(D(f);\\mathbb Q)$. It also acts by zero on every such group for a further $T$-invariant open subvariety $V\\subseteq D(f)$. Consequently $S_T^{-1}H^{\\mathrm{BM},T}_j(D(f);\\mathbb Q)=S_T^{-1}H^{\\mathrm{BM},T}_j(V;\\mathbb Q)=0$ for all $j$."
    ],
    "thm-qftx-finite-affine-atlas-bm-concentration": [
      null,
      "## Statement\n\nLet $T=(\\mathbb C^\\times)^r$ act algebraically on a separated finite-type complex variety $X$ that admits a finite cover by $T$-invariant affine open subvarieties. Let $F=X^T$ be the fixed-point subscheme, $i:F\\hookrightarrow X$ its closed inclusion, and let $S_T$ be the character multiplicative set in the localized equivariant Borel–Moore definition. Then in every homological degree $j$, proper pushforward induces an isomorphism\n$$\ni_*:S_T^{-1}H^{\\mathrm{BM},T}_j(F;\\mathbb Q)\\xrightarrow{\\ \\cong\\ }S_T^{-1}H^{\\mathrm{BM},T}_j(X;\\mathbb Q).\n$$\nNo compactness of $X$, normality hypothesis, or compact-orbit-type nilpotence hypothesis is required."
    ],
    "lem-qftx-fixed-embedding-bm-euler-self-intersection": [
      null,
      "## Statement\n\nLet $T=(\\mathbb C^\\times)^r$ act algebraically on a smooth separated finite-type complex variety $X$ with a finite invariant affine open cover. Let $F=X^T$, $i:F\\hookrightarrow X$, and $\\nu_F=TX|_F/TF$ be the complex normal bundle. Then $F$ is smooth, $T_xF=(T_xX)^T$ for every $x\\in F$, and every normal fiber has only nontrivial $T$-weights. On each fiber the restriction of $e_T(\\nu_F)$ to $BT$ is the product of the corresponding character classes with multiplicity. The closed regular embedding $i$ has an equivariant refined Gysin map $i^!:H^{\\mathrm{BM},T}_j(X;\\mathbb Q)\\to H^{\\mathrm{BM},T}_{j-2c}(F;\\mathbb Q)$ on each component of complex codimension $c$, normalized by $i^![X]_T=[F]_T$, with\n$$\ni^!i_*\\beta=e_T(\\nu_F)\\mathbin{\\cap}\\beta\n$$\nfor every $\\beta\\in H^{\\mathrm{BM},T}_*(F;\\mathbb Q)$, using the normalized Borel–Moore grading and complex orientation. If $F$ is proper, then $e_T(\\nu_F)$ is a unit in $S_T^{-1}H_T^*(F;\\mathbb Q)$. Empty components contribute no class, and a rank-zero normal bundle has Euler class $1$."
    ],
    "def-qftx-proper-fixed-locus-localized-pushforward": [
      null,
      "## Definition\n\nLet $T=(\\mathbb C^\\times)^r$ act on a smooth separated finite-type complex variety $X$ with a finite invariant affine open cover. Let $F=X^T$ be proper, $i:F\\hookrightarrow X$, $p_F:F\\to\\mathrm{pt}$, and $S_T$ the character multiplicative set. By the finite-affine-atlas concentration isomorphism, $i_*:S_T^{-1}H^{\\mathrm{BM},T}_j(F;\\mathbb Q)\\to S_T^{-1}H^{\\mathrm{BM},T}_j(X;\\mathbb Q)$ is invertible. Define the intrinsic localized pushforward\n$$\np^{\\mathrm{loc}}_*:=p_{F*}\\circ(i_*)^{-1}:S_T^{-1}H^{\\mathrm{BM},T}_j(X;\\mathbb Q)\\longrightarrow S_T^{-1}H^{\\mathrm{BM},T}_j(\\mathrm{pt};\\mathbb Q),\n$$\nwhere $p_{F*}$ is the genuine proper Borel–Moore pushforward. For a homogeneous $\\alpha\\in H_T^q(X;\\mathbb Q)$ and smooth complex dimension $d$, an allowed insertion is $\\alpha\\cap[X]_T\\in H^{\\mathrm{BM},T}_{2d-q}(X;\\mathbb Q)$; the fundamental class $[X]_T$ is the complex-oriented class, not the cohomological unit $1\\in H_T^0(X;\\mathbb Q)$. This construction does not define an ordinary pushforward along a nonproper map $X\\to\\mathrm{pt}$."
    ],
    "thm-qftx-proper-fixed-locus-noncompact-localization": [
      null,
      "## Statement\n\nLet $T=(\\mathbb C^\\times)^r$, $r\\geq0$, act algebraically on a smooth separated finite-type complex variety $X$ of pure complex dimension $d$. Assume $X$ has a finite $T$-invariant affine open cover and that its fixed-point subscheme $F=X^T$ is proper. Use Borel equivariant cohomology $H_T^q(X;\\mathbb Q)=H^q(E_K\\times_KX;\\mathbb Q)$ and the normalized Borel–Moore groups whose smooth $d$-dimensional fundamental class has degree $2d$. Let $\\chi_i$ be the coordinate characters, $u_i=c_1(L_{\\chi_i|_K})$, and $u_\\chi=\\sum_i n_i u_i$ for $\\chi(t_1,\\ldots,t_r)=\\prod_i t_i^{n_i}$. The multiplicative set $S_T$ is generated by $u_\\chi$ for all nontrivial characters. Write $F=\\coprod_a F_a$ for its finitely many connected components, $i_a:F_a\\hookrightarrow X$ for their inclusions, $d_a=\\dim_{\\mathbb C}F_a$, $c_a=d-d_a$, and $\\nu_a=TX|_{F_a}/TF_a$. Each $p_a:F_a\\to\\mathrm{pt}$ is proper. The localized pushforward is $p_*^{\\mathrm{loc}}=p_{F*}\\circ(i_*)^{-1}$, where $i_*=\\sum_a i_{a*}$ is the localized fixed-inclusion isomorphism and $p_F:F\\to\\mathrm{pt}$ is proper. For every homogeneous $\\alpha\\in H_T^q(X;\\mathbb Q)$, it satisfies\n$$ p_*^{\\mathrm{loc}}(\\alpha\\mathbin{\\cap}[X]_T)=\\sum_a p_{a*}\\left(\\frac{i_a^*\\alpha}{e_T(\\nu_a)}\\mathbin{\\cap}[F_a]_T\\right)\\quad\\text{in }S_T^{-1}H^{\\mathrm{BM},T}_{2d-q}(\\mathrm{pt};\\mathbb Q), $$\nwhere $p_{a}:F_a\\to\\mathrm{pt}$ is proper, $e_T(\\nu_a)$ is the zero-section Euler class with complex orientation, $[X]_T$ and $[F_a]_T$ are the complex-oriented fundamental classes, and division means multiplication by the localized inverse of $e_T(\\nu_a)$. If $X\\to\\mathrm{pt}$ is proper, $p_*^{\\mathrm{loc}}$ equals the genuine proper pushforward. The construction is independent of the chosen finite invariant affine cover and is compatible with proper equivariant maps between such smooth varieties with proper fixed loci. For finite $F$, the formula is the finite reciprocal-Euler sum; if $F=\\varnothing$, both sides are zero. A component with $c_a=0$ has denominator $1$. Each term has degree $2d-q$, since $e_T(\\nu_a)$ has degree $2c_a$ and $[F_a]_T$ has degree $2d_a$."
    ],
